From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:30:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CPU monitor from mastertune: the load and the voices in the
 OLED's corner, LEARN + tempo encoder

Ports mastertune 1.2.1's CPU monitor (its patches 0015, 0026, 0039, 0059, 0062, 0069, 0070) onto v1.3, without the
sampling profiler (0053, 0054). The core (processing/engines/cpu_stats_core.{h,cpp}: the collector, the OLED line,
the SysEx encoding) is mastertune's unchanged; the firmware side (cpu_stats.{h,cpp}) and the hooks are fitted to v1.3.

- Settings > CPU Monitor: Off, On, Alerts. On: one short line in the OLED's top left corner, "CPU 43% 24V", plus QL
  while the quality is lowered and a blinking VC while voices are cut; a popup on the 7-segment display; the numbers
  once a second as SysEx (command 0x10) to the computer on USB port 3, never to DIN. Alerts: only QL and VC.
- LEARN held + tempo encoder pressed switches it off and back on (the last of On and Alerts), in every view; neither
  the view nor the tempo popup gets that press. With Shift the press clears the tempo automation, as ever.
- Kept with the community settings as "cpuMonitor" (mastertune's name; its Profile is read as On). The shortcut's save
  runs in a task of its own that holds the SD card's resource, and keeps the startup song as it was: a song loaded
  but not saved doesn't become the one "Last saved" opens (RuntimeFeatureSettings::writeSettingsToFile() takes
  updateStartupSong, true everywhere else).
- Measured: each call of AudioEngine::routine() that renders in real time, the voices the CPU guard cuts short
  (killOneVoice(), terminateOneVoice(), forceReleaseOneVoice() when it starts a release; a voice that pass already
  stopped, OFF until it next renders, isn't counted again when it is picked again), the card reads of sample
  clusters. While off each hook costs one flag test.
- While a stem export renders offline the monitor pauses: the collector stops and the line goes, and the first window
  after the export starts after it. Before (and in mastertune 1.2.1) the window after an export counted the whole
  export as one gap of the audio routine and the line stayed up, frozen, over the export.
- The line goes on top of the finished image in a canvas of its own (OLED::sendMainImage()), so no screen's image is
  changed and it is gone as soon as the monitor is off; not over the screensaver.
